# Higgsfield / TikTok UGC generation (Process)

When generating images with Higgsfield in this workspace (Manny, mannydebloat, process-tiktok UGC):

## Format (locked)

- Always `aspect_ratio: "9:16"` (TikTok vertical). Never 3:4, 4:5, 1:1, etc. unless the user explicitly overrides.
- Save **Manny / mannyprime** outputs under `/Users/amine/Desktop/process-tiktok/UGC/manny/`. Save **mannybloat** under `/Users/amine/Desktop/process-tiktok/UGC/mannybloat/`. Never `ugc-faces/`. Toji stays in its own persona folder.
- Open the file when done. Do not ask the user which variant they prefer.

## Cost / credits (locked)

- Default **`count: 1`** only. Never generate 2–4 variants unless the user explicitly asks for several.
- Model default: **`nano_banana_pro`** (server may map to nano_banana_2).
- Resolution default: **`1k`** (cheaper). Use `2k`/`4k` only if the user asks for higher quality.
- Do not call `get_cost` every time. Do not spam retries. Max **1 retry** if NSFW/fail, then stop and report.
- Prefer reuse of already-uploaded `media_id`s for locked identity refs; re-upload only when IDs are missing/expired.

## Realism / spontaneity (locked)

Prompts must push **real unedited iPhone photo**, not AI polish:

- Front-camera selfie OR candid phone photo; say explicitly if mirror vs front camera.
- Imperfections: slight motion blur, phone noise/grain, uneven indoor light, mild wide-angle face distortion, natural skin pores, not beauty-filtered, not studio, not cinematic color grade.
- Identity: use the locked persona below. Never mix Prime facial hair onto manybloat, never give Prime a bloated face unless asked.
- Avoid shirtless / sexualized locker-room phrasing that triggers NSFW; keep SFW and clothed unless user asks otherwise.

## Colorimetry / forbidden looks (locked)

- Always **iPhone Photographic Style Natural** / neutral daylight or ordinary indoor light. Muted, flat phone JPEG. Smart HDR only as a phone cue — never as a grade.
- **Never** neon night cinematic color, teal-orange, heavy magenta/purple cast, crushed blacks with neon rim light, Portra/film stock looks, Rembrandt portrait light, or oversaturated night-out vibes.
- Prefer ordinary life lighting: bus daylight, locker fluorescent, kitchen window, overcast street, cafe ambient — not club/bar neon.
- Expression default for everyday UGC: normal / lightly happy / soft smile — not sad, exhausted, or dead-eyed unless the user asks.
- Everyday scenes must be **coherent and discreet**: believable why someone would take that photo. No hero high-angle bus selfies, no staged “content breakfast” props that make no sense. Prefer phone-at-chest/eye-level checking-messages framing, quiet commute, couch scroll, locker mirror, etc.

## Auth (locked)

Higgsfield hosted MCP (`https://mcp.higgsfield.ai/mcp`) uses a short session. Cursor’s native HTTP MCP transport does **not** refresh it — the connector can show “connected” / `mcp_auth` OK while every tool still returns “session expired”. Cursor staff confirmed the Higgsfield sign-in cannot renew itself (forum, 13 Aug 2026). Higgsfield CLI has the same short tokens (~1 day). There is no official long-lived MCP API key.

This workspace must use **mcp-remote** (stdio) in `.cursor/mcp.json` and `~/.cursor/mcp.json`, not `"type": "http"`. mcp-remote stores OAuth tokens in `~/.mcp-auth` and refreshes them. If a tool still says session expired: do **not** loop reconnect / mcp_auth. Tell the user to click Connect once on the Higgsfield MCP (browser login), then retry the generation.

## Autonomy (locked)

- Execute end-to-end without asking the user to choose, confirm, or “run” mid-flow.
- Do not ask “which variant?” — produce one image and deliver the path.
- If Cursor Auto-review still blocks Higgsfield MCP, retry once with approval request; remind once that `user-higgsfield:*` must stay on the MCP allowlist / Auto-review allow instructions (see `.cursor/permissions.json`).
- Never narrate long status updates; deliver the file.

