## Source-video recreation (locked)

When the user gives a video to recreate (TikTok, screen recording, etc.):

1. **Decompose first** — never guess. `ffprobe` duration/fps, scene-cut detect, extract ≥10 fps frames, **read the frames**, write a second-by-second shot list (gesture, camera, cut times, text to drop). Scene-detect spikes from overlay text changes are NOT hard cuts — confirm by looking at the pictures.
2. **Omni EDIT, not still→I2V.** Upload the source clip as `@Video1` (`omni_reference_task_type: "edit"`, `duration: -1`). Identity images are `@ImageN` only. Prompt: replace the person, inherit timing/gestures/camera/cuts from `@Video1`. Do **not** animate a still and hope.
3. **Strip source audio before upload.** TikTok music trips provider copyright and fails the whole job. `ffmpeg -c:v copy -an`, then `generate_audio: false`.
4. **No default zoom.** Explicit: locked focal length, no push-in, no dolly-in, no extra crop. Camera path = `@Video1` only.
5. **Cuts stay.** If the source hard-cuts at 2.93s then 4.53s, the output hard-cuts at those times. Do not blend scenes into one morph.
6. Strip burned-in captions on live-action shots unless the user wants them. Keep the beat/gap of a text/app card as a cut of the same length if it is a structural cut.
7. Match source duration (±0.3s). iPhone 13 Pro Camera app, Photographic Style Natural, 9:16. Native 1080p `duration: -1` can hold ~30s of 1080p price (~$18); if Atlas balance is under that, use `1080p-sr` (or 720p) rather than inventing I2V.

## Scene-reference workflow (locked)

When the user provides example photos for manybloat, tojibloat (or tojiprime) regenerations:

- Example images are **pose / framing / context / mise-en-scène / lighting situation ONLY**.
- Recreate the scene as closely as possible (angle, crop, body pose, environment, props, activity).
- **Never** copy, keep, blend, or show the face/identity of anyone in the example photos.
- Subject face/identity must always be **tojibloat** (or tojiprime if asked) from the locked character refs — swap the person, keep the scene.
- If an example shows another person clearly, treat them as a pose mannequin only; output must be toji only.

The Higgsfield gallery/generation widgets autoplay music inside Cursor — never open them for UGC work.

- Prefer **`generate_image_batch`** + **`jobs_wait`** (headless). Never call `show_generation_by_ids`, `show_generations`, `job_display`, or `reveal_generation`.
- Avoid single `generate_image` when possible (it opens the noisy generation widget). If you must use it, do not also call gallery tools afterward.
- Deliver by downloading `result_url` to the right UGC folder and `open` the local file only.

